      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 17,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene 005.6 — mapping the seven nexus points"
    },
    {
      "line": 19,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene meta:"
    },
    {
      "line": 20,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "location: Island & mainland vrill convergence sites"
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "time: year 312"
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "participants: Elyraen, Senareth, Giant council"
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "focus: Nephoretti and Giants map seven primary planetary Nexus Points, establishing a planetary-scale vrill communication network."
    },
    {
      "line": 24,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "continuity: Takes place 78 years after the Tidecaller mountain carving in scene 005.5"
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "presentation: undecided"
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nexus Points emerged through collective recognition rather than deliberate planning."
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Certain locations across the island and mainland simply felt more resonant than others."
    },
    {
      "line": 30,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Vrill-energy flowed more strongly there, consciousness-touch connected more readily, elements responded with greater cooperation."
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Giants had always known this instinctively—gathering in these places for meditation, for healing, for the deep communion that sustained their vast awareness."
    },
    {
      "line": 33,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But Nephoretti, with their more analytical approach, began mapping the pattern."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They identified seven primary sites where vrill-currents converged—places where the planetary consciousness seemed closest to surface, most accessible to beings who knew how to listen."
    },
    {
      "line": 36,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One lay at the island's center, deep within the Tidecaller mountain where underground water met volcanic heat."
    },
    {
      "line": 37,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Another crowned the highest peak of the crescent range, where mountain Giants had built their most ambitious obelisk cluster."
    },
    {
      "line": 38,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A third pulsed beneath the desert, accessible only through caves that copper-grey Giants had excavated over centuries."
    },
    {
      "line": 39,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Others scattered across forest valleys and coastal promontories."
    },
    {
      "line": 41,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Elyraen",
      "text": "\"Natural architecture,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 43,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The implications were staggering."
    },
    {
      "line": 44,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Buildings placed at Nexus Points could draw power directly from planetary vrill-flow."
    },
    {
      "line": 45,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Meditation practiced there accelerated consciousness development."
    },
    {
      "line": 46,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Healing became more effective."
    },
    {
      "line": 47,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Elements responded more readily to consciousness-touch and spoken frequencies."
    },
    {
      "line": 49,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "More importantly, the Nexus Points were interconnected."
    },
    {
      "line": 50,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Vrill-energy flowing through one could be sensed at others, creating a planetary-scale communication network for beings sensitive enough to perceive it."
    },
    {
      "line": 51,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Giants meditating at separate Nexus Points reported awareness of each other's presence, thoughts touching across distances that should have made such contact impossible."
    },
    {
      "line": 53,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Senareth",
      "text": "\"We're building the network,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 55,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Giants began constructing more deliberately—pyramids and obelisks positioned to enhance rather than interrupt natural vrill-flows."
    },
    {
      "line": 56,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Chambers carved to amplify rather than block planetary resonance."
    },
    {
      "line": 57,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Architecture that worked with Earth's consciousness rather than imposing foreign patterns upon it."
    },
    {
      "line": 59,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "By year four hundred, the seven Nexus Points anchored a web of resonance that spanned the known world."
    },
    {
      "line": 60,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Giants could communicate across continental distances through meditation at these sites."
    },
    {
      "line": 61,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Nephoretti could coordinate activities without needing to travel physically."
    },
    {
      "line": 62,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The planet itself seemed more responsive, more alive, more willing to collaborate with consciousness that approached it respectfully."
    },
    {
      "line": 64,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Garden had achieved something unprecedented: harmony between biological life, geological awareness, and planetary consciousness itself."
    },
    {
      "line": 66,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 68,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "year 448"
    }
  ],
